ll  return for the next installment of lock  and key thankfully most of the show's  main actors have confirmed they'll be  returning connor jessup was one of the  first actors to reaffirm his place in  the series even though his character  tyler locke leaves to go traveling at  the end of season 2. jessup told decider  in october 2021 i don't think when he  leaves at the end of season 2 that his  story is over to me it felt like a new  chapter but it didn't feel like a  resolution so there's still more for  tyler jessup will be joined by amelia  jones and jackson robert scott who play  his younger siblings kinsey and bodhi  darby stanchfield will also be returning  as their mom nina locke along with aaron  ashmore who plays duncan the locked  children's uncle meanwhile sherry sam  who plays ellie has been promoted to  series regular which means we might also  see more of kobe byrd who plays her son  rufus kevin durand will also be getting  more screen time as the revolutionary  war soldier captain frederick gideon  the dramatic second season of lock and  key came to a conclusion at the same  time as matheson academy's fall semester  at the end of the season finale nina  reveals that tyler is going traveling  over the winter break because he needs a  fresh start however the trailer for  season 3 places tyler squarely in the  middle of all the action alongside his  family so viewers can expect some time  to have a lapse between the second and  third seasons this means that the  earliest the series could be set is the  beginning of the spring semester with  tyler returning to finish his education  however it's also possible that more  time has passed taking viewers to the  end of the summer semester in tyler's  last few weeks at matheson academy  alternatively there could be less of a  school focus this season and the show  could be set entirely during the summer  holidays giving the lock family plenty  of time to deal with the show's latest  villain  for the last two 