shadows and tyler certainly appears to  have his memories back in the trailer  lock and key has always been a very  family oriented show however the events  of the season 2 finale have seen some  significant changes that will affect the  lock family dynamic plus tyler's bonds  with his siblings will undoubtedly  change after he forgets about magic  meanwhile nina will probably grow closer  to her children now that she knows about  magic as it's been a barrier between  them in previous seasons essentially  season 3 will focus on how the lox  navigate these changes and come together  to face captain gideon as show runner  meredith aberyl teased to collider the  third season focuses much more heavily  on the family they're going to face the  greatest threat they've had to face yet  that really bonds them in a way that  we've never seen before i can't say more  than that  kinsey and scott finally getting  together is something viewers of the  show have been waiting for ever since  our budding romance was dashed after  gabe swooped in and grabbed kinsey's  attention of course gabe turned out to  be the evil demon echo dodge so that  relationship was pretty much doomed from  the start as kinsey started to uncover  gabe's true identity she and scott fell  for each other again but their timing  wasn't great season two concluded with  the couple about to embark on a  long-distance relationship as scott  chose to attend film school in london  for a year before going to college  however scott's nickname for kinsey is  rocky road and that could be what the  couple are in for in season 3. in fact  netflix has yet to confirm that patrice  jones who plays scott is returning for  the third season and he doesn't appear  in the trailer other cast members have  posted behind the scenes photos for the  new season on instagram but jones is  strangely missing from the snaps that  said it's very possible jones return to  the show is just being kept under wraps  for dramatic effect and kinsey and scott  will end up back together in season  three  i'm here  you know if you need me  while patrice jones's return is up in  the air another lock love interest is  definitely due back in matheson for  season 3. brendan hines will once again  be featured as nina's on-again off-again  partner josh bennett the pair left their  relationship up in the air last season  when josh told nina he finally felt able  to move on from his wife's death and  commit to her properly she shut him down  in the season finale nina explained that  she wasn't ready and told him that she  needed more time before they could be  together however they certainly left  things open-ended with the possibility  for their relationship to blossom in  season 3. however if nina and josh do  rekindle their romance the fact that she  knows about magic might make things a  bit more difficult for them going  forward  it's always exciting when a lock and key  character reveals a new magical key and  thankfully there's more excitement to  come in season 3. duncan now has the  ability to make keys which is a good  skill to have with a super villain on  the loose according to the comics  created by joe hill there are still  plenty of keys left for the locks to  find and the trailer introduces a pretty  major one it looks like bodhi discovers  the time shift key allowing users to see  visions of the past when used in the  lock's grandfather clock this could  certainly come in handy as the lock  family tried to discover more about  captain gideon's past in order to defeat  him it also might come into play for  tyler when he gets his memories back as  he could see visions of his past self  using magic this key this  this key can make it so you never forget  season 2 also introduced a lot of new  keys to the show in addition to the ones  established in the first season fans are  certainly eager to see more keys like  the angel key which kinsey used in the  finale and was instrumental in helping  to defeat dodge  season 3 will be the lock family's last  paranormal adventure on netflix the show  hasn't been cancelled though as it was  always the plan to end the story after  three seasons according to  co-showrunners carlton hughes and  meredith averill lock and key will  naturally reach its conclusion at the  end of season 3 with the duo telling  deadline in a statement once we began  working on the series we felt three  seasons was the ideal length to bring  the story of the lock family and their  key house adventures to a satisfying  conclusion they also sang the praises of  writer joe hill and illustrator gabriel  rodriguez who created the lock and key  comic book series and joked we're  keeping the magical keys though for our  own personal use  since cues and abarrill have been  planning the conclusion of lock and keys  since the end of season 1 they should  have the opportunity to tie up all of  the show's loose threads so here's  hoping fans get everything they want to  see and more in season 3 of lock and key  the locking key showrunners have been  keeping quiet about a lot of the  particulars in the upcoming season but  the trailer does reveal a few extra  details for fans for one it looks like  gideon is creating an army while his  motives aren't clear the trailer  suggests he's coming for the keys and  possibly even key house itself however  gideon's evil plans appear to culminate  in a big battle between his army and the  lox  this is our house those keys belong to  us viewers can definitely expect to see  an epic showdown as tyler kinsey bodie  nina and duncan defend their home in the  keys in the battle to end all battles  this fight promises to be a satisfying  and dramatic conclusion to the final  season of lock and key  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite netflix shows are coming  soon subscribe to our youtube channel  and hit the bell so you don't miss a  single one  [Music]  you

